   and relicense it as part of the Work, under this license or any
   other. You confirm you have the right to give it. Contributions do
   not add markers under section 4.

7. Permission

   Permission only counts if it comes from me in writing: a message
   from the GitHub account ag0nyy-ops, or a message I send that
   clearly comes from me, that names who it is for, which repository
   or files, and what is allowed. It covers only what it names, and
   nothing more.

8. Accepting these terms

   The README of the Official Repository opens with a notice that the
   Work is covered by this license. Cloning, forking, downloading, building or running the Work, or
   using it in any way beyond viewing it in a web browser, means you
   accept these terms. If you don't accept them, your only rights are
   the ones the law gives you without a license.

9. Ending

   If you break these terms, every permission you had under this
   license ends automatically. You must then delete every copy of the
   Work you control, including clones, forks on GitHub or anywhere
   else, and any changed versions.

